        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a reference-class/persistence prior, then an equally weighted prior/proxy-bridge update. The historical sample is eight matching preliminary prints. The level component enters through the historical mean; momentum enters through the latest print and the earnings, hours, and output bridge. One-off and separate policy-mechanism adjustments are zero at the center, with their uncertainty retained in the interval. For this change series, compute dispersion from the values themselves: sigma = 2.112167 percentage points = sqrt(31.22875/(8-1)). A normal approximation gives an 80% half-width of 1.28*sigma = 2.703574. Centering on 0.9 gives -1.803574 to 3.603574, rounded to final bounds of -1.8% and 3.6%. Retain this empirical width because the bridge omits material compensation and sector details."
